--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- V2__seed_firm1.sql
--
-- Seed data for FIRM_CD=1 (the special firm) — a minimal but COHERENT slice that
-- makes the platform functional for one advisor: login + one household, its
-- client, accounts, holdings and the advisor's visibility grants.
--
-- Provenance : extracted from PROD (192.168.1.42 / ORCL12VM, schema GP) for real
--              FK/code consistency, then PII-SCRUBBED for this public-shareable
--              repo. IDs / codes / relationships are real; names, emails, tax ids,
--              account numbers and the password hash are synthetic or blanked.
-- Generated  : 2026-06-01. Applies on top of V1 (the GP baseline).
--
-- Scope (<=10 rows per table): 1 firm, 1 advisor (tim1/gwAdmin), 1 household,
-- 1 client, 3 accounts (+account_details), 6 entity-account roles, 5 view
-- policy-rule grants, 7 instruments, 10 positions.
--
-- THE tim1 LOGIN: the advisor entity is remapped to LDAP_UID='tim1' with
-- GW_ADMIN_FLAG=1 (this boolean IS "gwAdmin"), MFA off, active. Local geowealth
-- auth is SHA(LDAP_PSWD_HASH) OR SAML-broker via P1 (email auto-link). The P1
-- password (tim1 / *****) is NEVER committed: LDAP_PSWD_HASH is blanked here.
--   * SAML path: works as-is — email tim1@geowealth.int must match the P1 user's
--     email (adjust if P1 issues a different address).
--   * Direct DB login: set the hash LOCALLY, outside git, e.g.
--       UPDATE ENTITY_TBL SET LDAP_PSWD_HASH = '{SHA}'||<sha1(pwd) base64>
--       WHERE LDAP_UID='tim1';  -- compute with the platform's SHAPassword
--
-- NOTE: the React client/account DIRECTORIES are Elasticsearch-backed; after this
-- seed, re-index (RefreshClientSearcherTool) for the list views. Login, detail
-- pages and the policy-gated SQL reports work from this Oracle data directly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


